Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?phlink:=20phase=2006-03=20=E2=80=94=20block=20t?=
 =?UTF-8?q?hird-party=20cookies=20by=20default?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per PRD §6 PRIV-03, phlink blocks third-party cookies by default in
all profiles, not only incognito. Upstream defaults
prefs::kCookieControlsMode to CookieControlsMode::kIncognitoOnly;
phlink defaults it to CookieControlsMode::kBlockThirdParty.

Behavior:
- Regular and Guest profiles: 3p cookies blocked.
- Incognito: unchanged (still blocked, same as upstream).
- The user can still flip the toggle in Settings > Privacy. The pref
  is SYNCABLE so existing user choices win once Phase 9 brings
  encrypted profile import.

Refs PRD §6 (PRIV-03), plan 06-03.
---
 components/content_settings/core/browser/cookie_settings.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/content_settings/core/browser/cookie_settings.cc b/components/content_settings/core/browser/cookie_settings.cc
index fa0319e885d60..e7e533ebeece5 100644
--- a/components/content_settings/core/browser/cookie_settings.cc
+++ b/components/content_settings/core/browser/cookie_settings.cc
@@ -76,9 +76,13 @@ ContentSettingsForOneType CookieSettings::GetCookieSettings() const {
 
 void CookieSettings::RegisterProfilePrefs(
     user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable* registry) {
+  // phlink (PRD §6 PRIV-03 / plan 06-03): block third-party cookies by
+  // default in regular profiles too. Upstream defaults to
+  // `kIncognitoOnly` (block in incognito only). The user can still
+  // relax this via Settings > Privacy.
   registry->RegisterIntegerPref(
       prefs::kCookieControlsMode,
-      static_cast<int>(CookieControlsMode::kIncognitoOnly),
+      static_cast<int>(CookieControlsMode::kBlockThirdParty),
       user_prefs::PrefRegistrySyncable::SYNCABLE_PREF);
 }
 
